.TH MAILSLOT-CLI 1 "November 2026" "mailslot-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mailslot-cli \- send files to a Mailslot and receive them headless
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailslot-cli
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mailslot-cli
is the command-line companion of the Mailslot desktop app.
It uploads files, folders and standard input to a Mailslot link with resume, retry and duplicate detection,
and runs a headless receiver.
It does not need GTK.
.PP
A Mailslot link looks like
.BR mailslot://HOST:PORT/TOKEN .
The query parameters
.B tls=1
and
.BI pin= BASE64
select HTTPS and pin the server's public key.
.B label=NAME
names the link.
Plain
.BI http:// HOST : PORT / TOKEN /
URLs are accepted too.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR send " [" \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR "] [" \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR "] [" \-\-limit " " \fIRATE\fR "] [" \-\-json "] " \fIFILE\fR... " " \fILINK\fR
Upload files, folders (recursively) or standard input (use
.B \-
as the file).
Interrupted uploads resume from the offset the receiver reports.
Failed requests retry with backoff.
The SHA-256 is sent first, so the receiver verifies the file and skips content it already holds.
.B \-\-jobs
sets how many files go in parallel, and
.B \-\-limit
caps bandwidth (for example
.BR 2M ).
.B \-\-json
prints one JSON object per event.
The exit status is non-zero if any file failed.
.TP
.BR serve " [" \-\-bind " " \fIADDR\fR "] [" \-\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR "] [" \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR "] [" \-\-max\-mb " " \fIN\fR "]"
Run a headless receiver.
Prints one line,
.BR "URL http://HOST:PORT/TOKEN/" ,
to standard output once it is listening, then serves until SIGTERM or SIGINT.
Port mappings made through UPnP are removed on exit.
.TP
.BR watch " " \fIDIR\fR " " \fILINK\fR
Push new and changed files in a folder to a link.
.TP
.B pair
Print the link and a QR code for the configured receiver.
.TP
.B status
Show the configured receiver's state, link and recent transfers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ca.liminalhq.mailslot/config.toml
Settings shared with the desktop app. Flags override it.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ca.liminalhq.mailslot/
History and TLS certificate.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a file:
.PP
.RS
mailslot-cli send report.zip 'mailslot://192.168.1.20:8931/TOKEN'
.RE
.PP
Send a stream:
.PP
.RS
tar c project | mailslot-cli send \-\-name project.tar \- 'mailslot://192.168.1.20:8931/TOKEN'
.RE
.PP
Receive on a server:
.PP
.RS
mailslot-cli serve \-\-dir /srv/drop
.RE
.SH SECURITY
The link is the credential.
Anyone who has it can send files to the receiver.
Keep links private and use "New link" in the app, or restart
.B serve
with a new token, if one leaks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR sha256sum (1)
.PP
https://github.com/liminal-hq/mailslot
